Chapter: ConstraintShowGeneric
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A generic function constrained by `Show a =>` can call `show` on its
 type parameter. Dispatch threads the concrete type's derived
 `__show_T` as a function dictionary, so describe works for any type
 that derives Show.

Section: Types

  Shape =
    | Circle (Integer)
    | Rect (Integer) (Integer)
    deriving Show

Section: Body

  describe : Show a => a -> Text
  describe (x) = "[" & show x & "]"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (describe (Circle 5))
    print-line-uni (describe (Rect 3 4))
  end

